.TH MYSTRNCPY 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mystrncpy \- copy at most n characters of a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.PP
.BI "int mystrncpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src ", int " n ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mystrncpy()
copies at most
.I n
characters from
.I src
into
.IR dest ,
and always ends
.I dest
with a null byte. Unlike the standard
.BR strncpy (3),
the result is always null-terminated, so
.I dest
must have room for
.I n
+ 1 characters.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters copied.
